\ uart.ga - print a greeting on node 708's serial port
\
\ On GreenArrays' evaluation boards a USB serial port is wired to pins 17
\ and 1 of node 708, with both lines inverted: the pins idle low, and a
\ start bit is high. Node 708 sends each byte on pin 1 at 921600 baud, a
\ bit every 1085 ns, which UART takes:
\
\     gasim run --uart 708 examples/uart.ga

node 708
: main
    io b!                  \ B addresses io, to drive pin 1
    'message a!            \ A walks through the message
    @+ for @+ send next    \ the first word is the length - 1
    right a! @             \ wait forever on node 709

\ drives pin 1 high (3) or low (2) for a bit, 540 unexts of 2 ns each
: bit ( level ) !b 539 for unext ;

\ a start bit, 8 data bits from the lowest, and a stop bit, inverted
: send ( c )
    3 bit
    7 for dup 1 and 1 xor 2 + bit 2/ next drop
    2 bit ;

: message 13 , "Hello, world!" 10 ,
